  "description": "Default-off predictive coding for a dense foveal tensor. A fixed, shared four-field retinal encoder compresses each 8x8 native-detail tile into a small population code. A graph-resident self-training decoder learns the inverse by the existing local surprise-collapse rule. AllocentricWorldViewCell nodes retain earned latent priors across saccades. The adapter reports prediction error but cannot allocate attention: graph rules spend a bounded settlement budget on the unique largest decoder residual, bootstrap an unpredicted grounded surface only when residual evidence is absent, refuse exact score ties, and hand only graph-selected examples to the decoder. Unknown pixels remain absent through an explicit prediction mask.",
